# aside.view: one zone set aside, and what the message writes after it flowing at its right.
#
#   @{view:aside}
#   ```mermaid
#   flowchart TD
#       A[source] --> B[render]
#   ```
#
#   A paragraph, drawn in the column beside the diagram.
#
#   @{view:banner}
#   > [!TIP]
#   > a view too, while it fits
#
#   The rest of the message, once the diagram's height is filled, back at the full width.
#
# The zone is any side a split takes: a decorated zone, a bare mermaid fence, a markdown fence, a
# quote. What follows it flows in order, each paragraph, list or view WHOLE or not at all: the first
# that does not fit under the zone's height ends the column and stays where it was written. A
# table, a split or another aside ends it too.
#
# NO BODY, on purpose, as split.view: the carrier reads the zone and the engine lays it out
# (layout/aside.ts). Too narrow for a column of text beside the zone, the zone draws alone.
#
# Where this hook does not run, the decorator line is one harmless line of prose and the rest
# reads as written.
